PINGRecord.__init__ assigned self.ICMP_TYPE_DEST_UNREACBLE, a misspelling of the class constant
ICMP_TYPE_DEST_UNREACHABLE (ICMP type 3), so an ICMP destination-unreachable reply that reaches the filter
raised AttributeError instead of being recorded as state 3. __str__ and the class body already use the
correct spelling. The reply reaches the record only when the outer ICMP id is 0, because the vendored
filter matches on id (the lookup method, services/trex_service_icmp.py:38-54, keys on the reply's IP dst,
ICMP id, seq and VLANs; Scapy 2.4.3 leaves the id absent for type 3), so the fix affects that rare path
only. Unfixed upstream as of the v3.08 pin.

diff -ruN a/trex/common/services/trex_service_icmp.py b/trex/common/services/trex_service_icmp.py
--- a/trex/common/services/trex_service_icmp.py	2026-10-17 23:05:08.826903473 -0400
+++ b/trex/common/services/trex_service_icmp.py	2026-10-17 23:05:08.827046811 -0400
@@ -160,7 +160,7 @@
 
             if scapy_pkt['ICMP'].type == self.ICMP_TYPE_DEST_UNREACHABLE:
                 self.responder_ip = scapy_pkt['IP'].src
-                self.state        = self.ICMP_TYPE_DEST_UNREACBLE
+                self.state        = self.ICMP_TYPE_DEST_UNREACHABLE
                 return
 
 
